    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1410">

                <pb facs="1137" n="1127" xml:id="pg1127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.4552: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Callanan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-24T15:00:00+08:00">June 24, 1949—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:40 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>193. Registration Consular cars refused today unless submitted as for “former
                    American Consulate General” and “former Consul “General”. British colleague only
                    other similar case same treatment. Registration in personal name without
                    reference to status refused. Possibilities under consideration with Embassy’s
                    65, February 26, to Peiping<anchor n="70" xml:id="d1410-f1"/> in mind and no
                    intention denying Consular status.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 193; repeated Nanking 148, OffEmb Canton 89.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Callanan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
